{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "1CO",
  "chapter": 3,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "1CO.3.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.3.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I, brethren, could not speak to you as to spiritual, but as to carnal, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as to babes in Christ.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.3.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.3.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have fed you with milk, and not with meat: for hitherto ye were not able ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to bear it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", neither yet now are ye able.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.3.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.3.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For ye are yet carnal: for whereas ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " among you envying, and strife, and divisions, are ye not carnal, and walk as men?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.3.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.3.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For while one saith, I am of Paul; and another, I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of Apollos; are ye not carnal?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.3.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.3.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who then is Paul, and who ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Apollos, but ministers by whom ye believed, even as the Lord gave to every man?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.3.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.3.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have planted, Apollos watered: but God hath given the increase.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.3.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.3.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So then, neither is he that planteth any thing, neither he that watereth: but God that giveth the increase.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.3.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.3.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now he that planteth and he that watereth are one: and every man shall receive his own reward, according to his own labor.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.3.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.3.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For we are laborers together with God: ye are God's husbandry, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "ye are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " God's building.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.3.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.3.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "According to the grace of God which is given to me, as a wise master-builder, I have laid the foundation, and another buildeth upon it. But let every man take heed how he buildeth upon it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.3.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.3.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For other foundation can no man lay than that which is laid, which is Jesus Christ.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.3.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.3.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now if any man buildeth upon this foundation, gold, silver, precious stones, wood, hay, stubble;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.3.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.3.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Every man's work will be made manifest: for the day will declare it, because it will be revealed by fire; and the fire will try every man's work, of what sort it is.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.3.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.3.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If any man's work abideth which he hath built upon it, he shall receive a reward.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.3.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.3.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If any man's work shall be burned, he will suffer loss: but he himself shall be saved; yet so as by fire.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.3.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.3.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Know ye not that ye are the temple of God, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the Spirit of God dwelleth in you?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.3.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.3.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If any man defileth the temple of God, him will God destroy: for the temple of God is holy, which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "temple",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " ye are.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.3.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.3.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let no man deceive himself. If any man among you seemeth to be wise in this world, let him become a fool, that he may be wise.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.3.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.3.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the wisdom of this world is foolishness with God. For it is written, He taketh the wise in their own craftiness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.3.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.3.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And again, The Lord knoweth the thoughts of the wise, that they are vain.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.3.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.3.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore let no man glory in men: for all things are yours:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.3.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.3.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whether Paul, or Apollos, or Cephas, or the world, or life, or death, or things present, or things to come; all are yours;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.3.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.3.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And ye are Christ's; and Christ ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " God's.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
